items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-23----
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-24-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-25-## Statement
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-26-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-27-For a nonempty topological space $X$, the following are equivalent:
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-28-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md:29:1. $X$ is contractible.
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-30-2. The identity map $\operatorname{id}_X$ is nullhomotopic.
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-31-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-32-## Facts & Assumptions
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-33-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-34-**Given:** A nonempty topological space $X$.
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-35-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md:36:[A1] $X$ is contractible when every continuous map from $X$ to every topological space is nullhomotopic; a map is nullhomotopic when it is homotopic to a constant map ([[def-nullhomotopic-map-and-contractible-space]]).
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-37-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-38-[L1] Postcomposition by a continuous map preserves homotopies ([[thm-composition-respects-homotopy]], claim 2).
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-39-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-40-## Proof
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-41-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-42-**Proof technique:** direct.
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-43-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md:44:1.1 If $X$ is contractible, apply [A1] to the continuous map $\operatorname{id}_X:X\to X$ to conclude that $\operatorname{id}_X$ is nullhomotopic. [A1]
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-45-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-46-1.2 Conversely suppose $\operatorname{id}_X\simeq c_{x_0}$ for some $x_0\in X$, and let $f:X\to Y$ be any continuous map. Postcomposition by $f$ gives $f=f\circ\operatorname{id}_X\simeq f\circ c_{x_0}=c_{f(x_0)}$ by [L1]. Thus $f$ is nullhomotopic. [assume-hyp, L1, A1]
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md-47-
items/cor-contractible-iff-identity-nullhomotopic.md:48:2.1 Since $Y$ and $f$ in step 1.2 were arbitrary, every continuous map out of $X$ is nullhomotopic, so $X$ is contractible by [A1]. Together with step 1.1 this proves the equivalence. [step 1.1, step 1.2, A1] ∎
--
