items/ex-intervals-and-euclidean-spaces-are-contractible.md-45-1.1 For $x,c\in J$ and $t\in I$, $(1-t)x+tc$ lies between $x$ and $c$, so it lies in $J$ by [A1]. Thus $J$, viewed as a subset of $\mathbb R^1$, is convex. [A1, algebra]
