research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72781-+  compactness of the codomain suffices for closed graph to imply continuity;
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72782-+  Hausdorffness is needed for the converse. The stated two directions and the
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72783-+  proofs use those hypotheses correctly.
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log:72784:+- In `def-nullhomotopic-map-and-contractible-space`, the nonempty-space clause
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72785-+  "every map out of $X$ is nullhomotopic" is equivalent to the usual
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72786-+  identity-nullhomotopic definition. The ledger records this as a convention
research/audit/wave6-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-72787-+  delta, not a new theorem.
