research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12160-{"id":"def-path-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connected_space","https://www.mscsnet.mu.edu/~paul/Paper/4450102text.pdf"],"rationale":"The sources give paths, path-connectedness and path components in the standard unit-interval form. The item packages constant and reversed paths, concatenation and the empty/singleton conventions with local notation, so it is a semantic compilation. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12161-{"id":"def-locally-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mscsnet.mu.edu/~paul/Paper/4450102text.pdf"],"rationale":"Bankston's notes give the standard neighbourhood-base definitions of locally connected and locally path-connected spaces. The item states both together, requires the refining neighbourhood itself to be open, and records the equivalent basis language and the vacuous empty-space case. Source-record correction (Audit-Alpha, wave 3 A6): the WVU Math 581 §3.4 page originally recorded alongside it could not be opened by Alpha over https or http and was removed from the item and from this row; Alpha fetched the surviving URL at HTTP 200, and the item also retains the locally-connected-space reference, whose text Alpha read for the same definitions.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12162-{"id":"thm-locally-connected-iff-components-of-open-sets-are-open","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mscsnet.mu.edu/~paul/Paper/4450102text.pdf"],"rationale":"Bankston's notes state and prove the iff criterion for local connectedness via components of open subspaces, and the locally-connected-space reference states it verbatim as \"A space is locally connected if and only if for every open set U, the connected components of U (in the subspace topology) are open.\" The item adds the clopen conclusion for components of X and uses the library's explicit ambient/subspace conventions; its proof follows the sourced maximal-component argument. Source-record correction (Audit-Alpha, wave 3 A6): the WVU Math 581 §3.4 page originally recorded alongside them could not be opened by Alpha and was removed from the item and from this row; Alpha fetched both surviving sources at HTTP 200 and read the quoted clause.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12163-{"id":"thm-path-connected-implies-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/topology/connnotpathconn.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connected_space"],"rationale":"The sources state that every path-connected space is connected. The item also locates each path component inside a connected component and treats the empty-space convention; its proof adapts the standard continuous-image-and-common-basepoint union argument. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12164-{"id":"thm-connected-and-locally-path-connected-implies-path-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mscsnet.mu.edu/~paul/Paper/4450102text.pdf"],"rationale":"Bankston's notes and the locally-connected-space reference state the same theorem and prove it by showing path components are open and then using connectedness. The item makes the component partition and open-complement step explicit in its local phase format; this is a sourced proof adaptation. Source-record correction (Audit-Alpha, wave 3 A6): the WVU Math 581 §3.4 page originally recorded alongside them could not be opened by Alpha and was removed from the item and from this row; Alpha fetched both surviving sources at HTTP 200.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12165-{"id":"thm-a-linear-continuum-is-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear_continuum"],"rationale":"The linear-continuum reference states that the least-upper-bound and order-density conditions are exactly what make an ordered set connected in its order topology, and records that intervals and rays of a linear continuum are connected. The item includes every order-convex subset and supplies the standard supremum-cut proof with explicit endpoint and unbounded cases, so its statement is a semantic restatement and its proof an expanded adaptation. Source-record correction (Audit-Alpha, wave 3 A6): the UAB notes originally recorded here (people.cas.uab.edu/~jcmayer/TopNotes.pdf) are HTTP 404 together with the whole user directory, so they were removed from the item and from this row; Alpha fetched the surviving URL at HTTP 200 and confirmed it carries the cited connectedness content.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log:12166:{"id":"def-the-long-line","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-901-introduction-to-topology-fall-2004/e319b3a36ca774261b6b8c45e11804c2_notes_c.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_line_(topology)"],"rationale":"MIT's long-line notes and the reference article give the lexicographically ordered omega-one by half-open-unit-interval construction and its order topology. The item distinguishes the closed long ray, open long ray and doubled long line and fixes the endpoint/gluing conventions, so it is a semantic compilation. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log:12167:{"id":"thm-the-long-line-is-a-connected-linear-continuum","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/18-901-introduction-to-topology-fall-2004/e319b3a36ca774261b6b8c45e11804c2_notes_c.pdf"],"rationale":"MIT's notes state that the long line is a path-connected linear continuum and use countable ordinal boundedness in its analysis. The item instead proves the closed long ray is a linear continuum and connected, and separately audits the countable-choice dependence of boundedness for at-most-countable subsets; that set-theoretically explicit proof is local. The URL was retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12168-{"id":"lem-the-oscillating-zigzag-curve","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/topology/connnotpathconn.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topologist%27s_sine_curve"],"rationale":"The sources develop the established topologist's-sine-curve pattern: a path-connected oscillating graph whose closure adds a vertical segment and is connected but not path-connected or locally connected. The item replaces sine by an explicitly piecewise-linear zigzag with the same mathematical mechanism, making it a recoverable alteration rather than genuine novelty; its detailed formula, closure computation and no-path proof are locally generated. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12169-{"id":"rem-connectedness-conventions","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connected_space","https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/004R"],"rationale":"The sources expose the competing empty-space conventions and the standard distinctions among separated sets, connectedness, path-connectedness and local connectedness. The remark is a library-specific compilation of those established conventions and scope choices. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12170-{"id":"fs-a-connected-space-is-path-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/topology/connnotpathconn.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topologist%27s_sine_curve"],"rationale":"The sources explicitly document connected spaces that are not path-connected, including the topologist's sine curve and its closure. The item instantiates that standard refutation with the library's piecewise-linear zigzag closure; the short dependency-indexed refutation is local. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12171-{"id":"fs-the-closure-of-a-path-connected-set-is-path-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://kconrad.math.uconn.edu/blurbs/topology/connnotpathconn.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topologist%27s_sine_curve"],"rationale":"The sources give the closed topologist's sine curve as the closure of an oscillating path-connected graph and state that the closure is not path-connected. The item uses the piecewise-linear zigzag analogue and delegates the computation to its local lemma, so the refutation text is locally generated. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12172-{"id":"fs-a-connected-space-is-locally-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://www.mscsnet.mu.edu/~paul/Paper/4450102text.pdf","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topologist%27s_sine_curve"],"rationale":"The sources identify the topologist's sine curve as connected but not locally connected. The item transfers the same obstruction to the library's polygonal zigzag closure and relies on the locally proved witness, so the exact refutation is local while the mathematical phenomenon is established. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-12173-{"id":"fs-an-intersection-of-connected-sets-is-connected","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-generated","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connected_space"],"rationale":"The source expressly notes that intersections of connected sets need not be connected. The item supplies a concrete unit-square-boundary witness with nonempty intersection and verifies both three-sided sets by standard union arguments; that witness proof is local. The URL was retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
