research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-386779-+{"id":"def-baire-space","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_space"],"rationale":"The source defines a Baire space by density of every countable intersection of dense open sets and records the equivalent nonempty-open-set formulation. The item fixes zero-based indexing and withholds the general meagre-set vocabulary unavailable in its dependency graph, so it is a semantic restatement. The URL was retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200). The sequence citation's domain mismatch is reported separately.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-386780-+{"id":"thm-baire-category-locally-compact-hausdorff","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08ZQ","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baire_category_theorem"],"rationale":"Stacks Lemma 5.13.1 proves that every locally quasi-compact Hausdorff space is Baire by nested compact closures, and the second source records the locally compact Hausdorff form. The item makes Dependent Choice sufficient and explicit and routes the stagewise construction through its bridge lemma, so its statement and proof are sourced alterations. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200). The general-sequence citation defect is reported separately.","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-386781-+{"id":"def-one-point-compactification","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"not-applicable","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090A","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandroff_extension"],"rationale":"The sources give the topology obtained by adjoining one point and using complements of closed compact subsets as its neighbourhoods. The item constructs a guaranteed fresh point, works without assuming Hausdorffness, and verifies the topology inline, so it is a semantic compilation rather than an exact transcription. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
research/audit/wave4-dispatch/audit-beta-topology.log-386782-+{"id":"thm-one-point-compactification-properties","statement":"ai-altered","proof":"ai-altered","evidence":"semantic-source","urls":["https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/090A","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexandroff_extension"],"rationale":"The sources give compactness, the open embedded copy, density for noncompact X, and the Hausdorff criterion for the one-point compactification. The item packages all directions under its weak local-compactness convention and expands the standard compact-complement separation proof, so both components are sourced alterations. Both URLs were retrieved through the model-side web route (HTTP 200).","alpha_concurred":false,"at":"2026-08-04"}
